ated surfactants in surface and drinking waters</article-title><source>Environ Sci Pollut Res Int</source><volume>13</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17067024</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b34-ehp0116-000651"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taniyasu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kannan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>So</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Gulkowska</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinclair</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Okazawa</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Analysis of fluorotelomer alcohols, fluorotelomer acids, and short- and long-chain perfluorinated acids in water and biota</article-title><source>J Chromatogr A</source><volume>1093</volume><issue>1&#x02013;2</issue><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16233874</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b35-ehp0116-000651"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilhelm</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kraft</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rauchfuss</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>H&#x000f6;lzer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><comment>In press</comment><article-title>Assessment and management of the first German case of a contamination with perfluorinated compounds (PFC) in the region Sauerland, North Rhine-Westphalia</article-title><source>J Toxicol Environ Health A</source></citation></ref><ref id="b36-ehp0116-000651"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yamashita</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Kannan</surname><given-names>K</given-n